{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pulls/12333","id":4156106601,"node_id":"PR_kwDOOCjvss73uSdp","html_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12333","diff_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12333.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ai-dynamo/dynamo/pull/12333.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/issues/12333","number":12333,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(llm): recover truncated glm47 <tool_call> blocks on finish_reason=length","user":{"login":"peilii","id":76031090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDMxMDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76031090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii","html_url":"https://github.com/peilii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nGLM-5.2 emits tool calls as XML (`<tool_call>fn<arg_key>k</arg_key><arg_value>v</arg_value></tool_call>`). When `max_tokens` truncates the response inside a `<tool_call>` block, the partial block is silently dropped and the client receives an incomplete turn. This PR recovers the truncated block as raw content in both the non-streaming and streaming paths.\n\n### Non-streaming (`aggregator.rs`)\n\nBefore calling the parser, `rfind(\"<tool_call>\")` locates the last opened block. If no `</tool_call>` follows it on a `finish_reason=length` response, the tail is saved. After parsing (which may extract a complete first tool call), the tail is appended to `choice.text` if not already present. The first complete tool call is returned as a structured `tool_calls` entry; the truncated second block is returned as raw content.\n\n### Streaming (`preprocessor.rs`)\n\nA per-choice `ChoiceRecovery` struct buffers raw input text in the jail-input stream. On `finish_reason=length`, the same `rfind` logic finds the last incomplete block and emits it as a synthetic content delta before the finish chunk. Using `rfind` means already-parsed complete blocks are never duplicated as raw content.\n\n### Note on fix location\n\nThe recovery lives in the frontend stream rather than inside `dynamo-parsers` because the parser does not see SSE protocol events like `finish_reason`. By the time `finish_reason=length` arrives, the parser's internal state for the partial block has already been discarded. Pushing this into the parser would require a new `flush_on_truncation()` interface in `dynamo-parsers` and threading the truncation signal into the jail — a larger change deferred to a follow-up. Deferring to @keivenc for parser-level feedback.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo build -p dynamo-llm`: clean, zero warnings\n- `cargo test -p dynamo-llm`: all tests pass\n- `cargo clippy --no-deps -p dynamo-llm -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `cargo fmt --check -p dynamo-llm`: clean\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved GLM-47 handling of truncated tool calls in streaming responses.\n  * Preserved incomplete tool-call content when responses end due to length limits.\n  * Prevented duplicated content and ensured finish indicators appear only once.\n  * Improved handling of truncated responses containing multilingual text and emoji.\n\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for streaming recovery, multiple tool calls, clean completions, and UTF-8 boundaries.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-07-29T00:23:48Z","updated_at":"2026-08-10T23:51:40Z","closed_at":"2026-08-10T23:51:39Z","merged_at":"2026-08-10T23:51:39Z","merge_commit_sha":"3845b92ce644ee3761356214fe5f283ece7c7994","assignees":[{"login":"peilii","id":76031090,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDMxMDkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76031090?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii","html_url":"https://github.com/peilii","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/peilii/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":8461525019,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOCjvss8AAAAB-FigGw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/labels/size/XL","name":"size/XL","color":"C32607","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8582537231,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOCjvss8AAAAB_48gDw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/labels/fix","name":"fix","color":"158c01","default":false,"description":null,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9261210107,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOCjvss8AAAACKALZ-w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ai-dynamo/dynamo/labels/frontend","name":"frontend","color":"70d0ff","default":false,"description":"`python -m dynamo.frontend` and `dynamo-run in=http|text|grpc`","archived_at":null,"archived_by":nul